  <section>
    <h2>What is the Rich Text Editor, and why now?</h2>
    <p>The Rich Text Editor shipped as part of a larger Telegram update announced alongside Communities, Ephemeral Bot Messages, and search across 350 million GIFs. Its purpose is straightforward: let people write long, structured text — an announcement, a guide, internal documentation, or an article-style post — directly inside Telegram, without reaching for an outside tool.</p>
    <p>This isn't the same as Telegram's older basic formatting (bold, italic, spoilers) — it's a full visual editor that supports headings, tables, and inline media placed directly inside the text flow. For the fuller feature list, see <a href="/en/blog/telegram-premium-features">what Telegram Premium actually gives you</a> — that guide was written in May 2026, before this feature existed.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What elements can you add?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Headings</strong> — to break text into sections;</li>
      <li><strong>Tables</strong> — for pricing, comparisons, or tabular data;</li>
      <li><strong>Lists</strong> — numbered and bulleted;</li>
      <li><strong>Quotes and code blocks</strong> — for technical or documentation-style content;</li>
      <li><strong>Formulas</strong> — for math or scientific content;</li>
      <li><strong>Photos and videos</strong> — anywhere inside the text, not just at the start or end.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to open it, step by step</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Check your Premium subscription</strong> — the feature only unlocks with an active subscription.</li>
      <li><strong>Start typing a message</strong> — in any chat, group, or channel.</li>
      <li><strong>Tap the ⛶ icon</strong> — it appears in the text field once you've typed more than 3 lines, and opens the full-screen editor.</li>
      <li><strong>Add elements</strong> — pick a heading, table, list, or code block, and drop photos or videos into the text.</li>
      <li><strong>Send it</strong> — the message goes out fully formatted.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How does the Cocoon AI assistant work?</h2>
    <p>Built into the editor are AI tools based on Telegram's <strong>Cocoon</strong> technology, which help generate or edit text, tables, and formulas. Telegram states these tools are designed with a particular focus on privacy — meaning your text isn't left sitting on third-party servers.</p>
  </section>

